{
  "version": 1,
  "license": "CC0-1.0",
  "about": {
    "summary": "What Strafe Desktop needs to recognise a game from a running process on this device. Written by Strafe contributors from public knowledge (not copied from Discord's, SteamDB's or any other compiled list) and released under CC0. Read by both shells: electron/src/games (Linux) and src-tauri/src/games (Windows, macOS). Nothing here is fetched at runtime.",
    "patterns": "launchers, helpers and interpreters are lists of patterns, compared case-insensitively. A pattern without '/' is an executable basename, where '*' stands for any run of characters (so 'vc_redist*.exe'). A pattern with '/' is a path segment: it matches when the process's path, with '\\' turned into '/', contains it (so '/_commonredist/').",
    "launchers": "Store clients and their services: never a game on their own, and never offered when adding a game. A game started from one is recognised by its own process.",
    "launcherLabels": "Names a launcher gives its whole Wine prefix in Lutris (GAME_NAME). A process carrying one of these is matched by its own path or the curated list instead.",
    "helpers": "Processes that are never the game even inside a game's folder: crash reporters, installers, anti-cheat services, Wine's own system processes.",
    "interpreters": "Runtimes that run many different programs. Never offered when adding a game (a Wine program is offered by its own name instead).",
    "wineLoaders": "Executable basenames of Wine and Proton's loader. Such a process is the Windows program named by its first argument.",
    "steamToolAppids": "Steam app ids that are tools, runtimes or always-on applications, never games.",
    "steamToolNamePrefixes": "Steam app names that start with one of these (case-insensitive) are tools too, for the ones the id list does not know yet.",
    "curated": "Games recognised by name: { id, name, match: [{ os: win32|darwin|linux, exe: basename (case-insensitive, exact), pathContains?: path segment (case-insensitive, '/' separators), cmdlineAny?: [substring of one argument (case-sensitive)] }] }. Entries are tried in this order and the first that matches wins. cmdlineAny is only allowed on java/javaw rules: no other process's command line is read. On Linux a Wine process is matched against the win32 rules by the program Wine runs."
  },
